imply by  searching in google  so we have a z value to be 7.09 and the  critical value to be 1.645  since 7.09 is greater than 1.645 we can  simply reject the null hypothesis and  come to a conclusion that there is  enough evidence to support that the mean  of the class is greater than 70.  this is how you can use a z value to  arrive at a proper conclusion  now let's move on to t-test  t-test statistics is a method of testing  hypothesis about the mean of a small  sample drawn from the normally  distributed population  when the population standard deviation  is not known  in this case the data is continuous  the formula to calculate a t value is x  bar minus mu divided by s divided by  root n  where x bar is the sample mean s is the  sample standard deviation n is the  sample size and mu is the population  mean  let's discuss with the help of an  example  suppose the store wants to improve its  sales the previous sales data shows that  the average sales of thirty percent was  forty dollar per sale  after some corporate training the  current data showed an average sale of  dollar sixty per transaction  as the standard division is given to be  twenty dollar we have to calculate the t  value and we have to arrive at a  conclusion that did training improve the  sales or not  so in this case we have the sample mean  to be 60 standard deviation to be 20 the  sample size is taken as 30 and the  population mean is 40.  putting all the values in the formula  will arrive at a value of 5.47  in this case also we assume the  significance value to be 0.05  now moving from right to left in a z  table  the critical value will come out to be  1.711  which is less than 5.47 so in this case  also we can reject the null hypothesis  and we can conclude that the training  did affect the sales  and the training was helpful  so with this we come to an end to this  tutorial i hope this tutorial was useful  for you and you understood what is that  test and t-test is and how it can be  used